`twisted.conch.ssh.keys.Key.verify` now takes an optional `signatureType` argument and raises `BadSignatureAlgorithmError` if it does not match the algorithm embedded in the signature. `twisted.conch.checkers` now passes the algorithm name from `MSG_USERAUTH_REQUEST` when verifying public key signatures, so a signature made under one algorithm can no longer be presented as if it had been made using a different one.
